  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>…</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>.</mo><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></msub></math> are <math><mn>20</mn></math> skew-symmetric matrices of same order and <math><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></msup></math>, then the sum of the principal diagonal elements of matrix&nbsp;<math><mi>B</mi></math> is equal to",
